  "how_to_reproduce": "python papers/paper-09-structured-epistemic-learning/top_tier/demonstrate_d1v1_2_build_toggle.py --dump-designs <DIR>   # orion-capable build; then the same script --refit <DIR> under a different build of the numerical stack. Side A used /Users/billy/miniforge3/bin/python3.13; sides B and C used /Users/billy/miniforge3/envs/gnn_trading/bin/python and /Users/billy/miniforge3/envs/particle_tracking_python/bin/python.",
  "mechanistic_finding": "The deciding factor is the binary build of the numerical stack executing lbfgs, beneath the recorded version manifest. Given bit-identical design inputs, bit-identical labels, identical scipy (1.17.1) and scikit-learn (1.8.0) versions, and the identical frozen selection rule selecting logistic-C1 on every side: the conda CPython 3.13.12 / NumPy 2.4.4 stack converges in 480 lbfgs iterations to the coefficient vector whose canary is 494186ed... and reproduces the archived 0.50 with zero per-case flips on all four arms; the conda CPython 3.11.15 / NumPy 2.4.3 stacks (two independently installed envs, bit-identical canaries 9b56df6a...) converge in 439 iterations to a different terminal vector that flips exactly the 32 sub-margin UNRESOLVED-truth protected cases and lands 0.75. Both sides converge cleanly (no warnings) and are exactly deterministic within build. The archived 0.50 and the divergent 0.75 are the two attractor terminals of a degenerate comparator whose decision boundary sits inside a 0.014-wide probability band on 32 of 128 protected cases; last-bit coefficient differences between builds are amplified across that band. Toggling the executing build toggles the number: that is the one-factor reproduction the reopened box demands.",
